6. THE LOGIC LEVELS on the makers' printed rows (MODEL from PRINTED figures; each controller's rail from its AP2112K-3.3: 98.5 % to
   101.5 % PRINTED with the load regulation -1 to +1 %/A PRINTED at the rail's declared 0.25 A: 3.2422 V to 3.3577 V, inside the gate's 1.65 to
   5.5 V row; a resistor that names no tolerance at +-5 % (ASSUMPTION))
   the vote: a voter's high at least 2.8422 V (VDD - 0.4 V at 8 mA, DS12110 Table 158) against the SN74LVC1G08's VIH 2.0 V; a voter in reset
     or dark: its input at most 0.0551 V (II 5 uA and the pin's 250 nA into 10.5 kOhm) against VIL 0.8 V; the voter's output current at
     most 0.353 mA (inside Table 158's 8 mA)
   SHDN lifted by the vote: at least 2.3773 V (the gate's VCC - 0.15 V at -100 uA, -40 to 125 C, less the 1N4148W's 0.715 V at 1 mA, both
     PRINTED; the diode's figure is printed at 25 C and the diode carries at most 45.3 uA here, so the 1 mA maximum is taken as its bound
     at the kit's -20 C floor too: ASSUMPTION, margin 0.377 V) against the TCAN334's VIH 2.0 V; the gate's load 45.3 uA, inside its 100 uA row
   SHDN at rest: at most 0.420 V (the pin's 4 uA out, IIL PRINTED, into 105 kOhm) against VIL 0.8 V (round 6's figure, unchanged)
   the observation (the reader's own pull-up enabled, RPU 30 to 50 kOhm PRINTED, a firmware row): TXD high reads at least 2.8422 V
     against 0.7 VDD = 2.3504 V at the reader's highest rail; TXD low reads at most 0.6040 V (VOL 0.4 V plus the divider of 2222 Ohm against
     RPU's least) against 0.3 VDD = 0.9727 V at the reader's lowest rail (DS12110 Table 157, CMOS levels, tested)
   a FAULTY READER driving its input (an output where an input belongs): at most 1.646 mA through its 2178 Ohm (with the other reader's
     pull-up), inside the 8 mA at which Table 158 holds TXD at VDD - 0.4 V or 0.4 V: the TXD stays at least 2.8422 V high (TCAN334 TXD VIH
     2.0 V; the other reader's VIH 2.3504 V) or at most 0.4 V low (TCAN334 VIL 0.8 V): one reader can neither move the transceiver's input
     nor what the other reader sees, so it cannot frame a healthy controller (the vote still needs the other reader's agreement)
   the dark cases: a dark TARGET's gate takes at most 10 uA per input from a voter (Ioff PRINTED, 5.5 V) and its transceiver's TXD at most
     2.5 uA (ILKG(OFF) PRINTED); a dark target cannot drive its fabric (its transceiver's VCC is its own rail). A dark target's TXD reads
     recessive at a reader while its unpowered pins sink less than 17.1 uA (the reader's RPU against its VIH): ST prints no leakage for an
     unpowered FT pin (DS12110 Rev 10 prints none; Table 120's note 3 says only that no positive injection occurs under the maximum),
     so a dark target's TXD is UNDEFINED at its readers
     and the attribution must never act on a TXD reading alone (a condition for L4A-55). A dark VOTER's input reads low through 10 kOhm
   the controller's own rail: round 6's bounded state 0.1739 A less its limiters' pull-ups 0.678 mA, plus its two gates' ICC 10 uA each
     (PRINTED), its four readings' pull-ups 0.104 mA each while dominant, and the larger of two of its votes asserted at 0.353 mA each (one
     peer contained on both fabrics) and its own gate's two inputs high from the peers' lower rails (the self-test's V phase on it:
     delta ICC 500 uA an input at VCC - 0.6 V, PRINTED, taken per input), all at once: at most 0.1747 A (MODEL; a labelled scenario for
     the coordinator's C-DEV, no case row changed here)
   all levels hold: yes

7. THE VOTE PATH'S IN-SERVICE SELF-TEST (drafted for the firmware stage as rows of the contract; nothing applied)
   One transceiver at a time is tested, never while a fabric is down, so the quorum keeps its three controllers on the other fabric
   and two on the tested one. Per transceiver (6) four phases, one per window of FW-B22's 100 ms schedule (DRAFTED), every 1 window(s):
     S  the target's own SHDN request alone      -> the transceiver silenced
     P1 the next controller's vote alone         -> the transceiver not silenced
     P2 the one after's vote alone               -> the transceiver not silenced
     V  both peers' votes                        -> the transceiver silenced
   in each phase the asserting party holds its line from 10 ms after the window opens to 10 ms before it closes (80 ms held), and
   the three controllers send that window's state frames on the tested fabric at its middle; the evidence of a silence is THREE
   independent readings: the target's attempt shows on its TXD at both readers (its start of frame and error flag) while neither
   receives a frame of it on that fabric, and the target's own receiver hears neither peer there (SHDN high turns driver AND receiver
   off and holds RXD high, TCAN334 Table 6-5 PRINTED); the evidence of no silence is the target's frame received by both and both
   peers' frames received by it. Precondition: in the previous window every controller heard every other on both fabrics and no
   attribution is running; else the phase is skipped, and every controller publishes its phase counter, so a skip or a stall is seen
   TIMING on printed figures:
     silence takes effect within 10.020 us of the second vote: the GPIO edge 16.6 ns (speed 00 at 50 pF, DS12110 Table 160 PRINTED) + the
       gate's 3.6 ns (tpd at 3.3 V +- 0.3 V, -40 to 85 C, PRINTED; board B's air 76.25 C inside 85 C) + tMODE 10 us (PRINTED maximum)
     it ends within 13.01 us of the release: SD's 105 kOhm against 20 pF (ASSUMPTION: TI prints no SHDN capacitance; the two diodes' CT
       2 pF each PRINTED) down to VIL, + tMODE 10 us; the vote line's edge 6.18 ns/V against the gate's 10 ns/V limit at 50 pF
       (C_VOTE 50 pF, a Layer 10 bound named here: Ci 4 pF and CIO 5 pF PRINTED, the trace the rest)
     the guard 10 ms covers FW-B22's queue 4.6 ms (MODEL), two crystals' drift over a window 4.0 us (+-20 ppm, the fitted crystal's sheet
       as STM32H743-COMPATIBILITY.md section 7 reads it) and the slower hardware edge: margin 5.383 ms
     a reader's copy of a TXD edge rises or falls in about 225 ns (10 to 90 %, 2.2 kOhm against 46 pF: ASSUMPTION, a Layer 10 bound),
       the same on both edges, so a dominant interval keeps its length at the reader to within that time
   THE INTERVAL: one cycle is 6 transceivers x 4 phases x 1 window(s) x 100 ms = 2.4000 s; a latent fault of the vote path is exercised
     within one cycle, its phase is judged in the next window, and it is declared on its 2. consecutive failure (one corrupted frame
     never declares one): DETECTED WITHIN 5.00 s of its onset (MODEL on the printed timing above and the DRAFTED 100 ms window)
   the self-test's cost: two phases in four silence one transceiver for 80 ms; with DAR = 1 (L9T5-D2) the target's one attempt in such
     a phase raises its transmit error count by 8, 16 a cycle per transceiver, against at least 22 successful frames that lower it by 1
     each: the count stays bounded and error-active (the protocol's fault confinement)
   the target's probe and that bound rest on DAR = 1, and the records disagree (finding W137-F1, for L4A-55 and Layer 5): the
     contract draft reads "FDCAN_CCCR.DAR = 1" and the compatibility page's ES0392 2.24.5 row "firmware does not use DAR". With DAR = 0
     the target sends nothing on the tested fabric in its silenced phases (an automatic retry would raise its count by 8 at every
     attempt), so the silence rests on two readings, not three (no frame of it, its receiver hearing neither peer), same interval
   timing and cost hold: yes
   THE SELF-TEST'S OWN FAULTS, element by element (per transceiver; the residuals are named, none defeats the containment alone):
     a vote output, its line or its gate input  stuck low or open              the target cannot be silenced by the vote                    V fails                      within 5.00 s
     a vote output, its line or its gate input  stuck high                     the other peer alone silences the target                     the other peer's P fails     within 5.00 s
     a vote pull-down (10 kOhm)                 short                          as its vote stuck low                                        V fails                      within 5.00 s
     a vote pull-down (10 kOhm)                 open                           the input floats only while its voter is in reset or dark    NOT in service: RESIDUAL     none
     the 2-of-2 gate                            output stuck low               the target cannot be silenced by the vote                    V fails                      within 5.00 s
     the 2-of-2 gate                            output stuck high              the target silenced on that fabric at once (IOHA row 7)      its frames absent            within one window (100 ms)
     the gate's 100 nF                          short                          the target's own rail shorted: the target dark (IOHA row 3)  its frames absent            within one window (100 ms)
     the vote diode                             open                           the target cannot be silenced by the vote                    V fails                      within 5.00 s
     the vote diode                             short                          the gate's low holds SD: the target's own request fails      S fails                      within 5.00 s
     the own-request diode                      open                           the target's own request fails                               S fails                      within 5.00 s
     the own-request diode                      short                          the request pin's low holds SD: the vote fails               V fails                      within 5.00 s
     SD's 100 kOhm                              open                           SD rests on the pin's internal pull-down (TI: a fall-back)   NOT in service: RESIDUAL     none
     the transceiver's SHDN input               ignored                        neither the request nor the vote silences                    S and V fail                 within 5.00 s
     an isolation resistor                      open                           its reader sees no TXD edge while the frames arrive          continuous reading           within 3 windows (300 ms): every window carries a frame of each controller on each fabric
     an isolation resistor                      short                          isolation lost: a faulty reader could then move the TXD      NOT in service: RESIDUAL     none
     a reading pin or its input stage           stuck                          the two readers of one TXD disagree                          continuous reading           within 3 windows (300 ms): every window carries a frame of each controller on each fabric
     a node's test schedule                     stalled or out of turn         phases fail or counters disagree                             the published phase counter  within one window (100 ms)
     a node's verdict                           wrong (two-faced or corrupted) outvoted: verdicts are taken 2 of 3                          the confirmation             within 5.00 s
   coverage: every one of the 54 parts of the six vote and twelve observation paths (gates, pull-downs, isolation resistors, both
     diodes, SD's resistor, the gates' capacitors) is the subject of a row, and every part canmb adds or re-uses is among them: yes
   the residuals, each needing further faults: an open vote pull-down acts only while its voter is in reset or dark AND the other peer
     votes wrongly; a shorted isolation resistor matters only when its reader also drives its input (and then both readers see the moved
     line, which the 2-of-2 vote then silences: the bus is freed, the target loses one fabric); an open SD resistor leaves the transceiver
     on TI's internal pull-down; a voter that resets while asserting gives the gate a slow edge (10 kOhm against the line) outside the
     gate's 10 ns/V limit: the output may chatter for that edge, and only while the other peer asserts, so it can only end a silence early

